      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bonadelle Ranchos-Madera Ranchos grew from two historic land grants, the Bonadelle and Madera Ranchos, that once covered the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/california_bonadelle-ranchos-madera-ranchos",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community was planned in the 1970s, becoming one of California’s first master‑planned communities in the Central Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/california_bonadelle-ranchos-madera-ranchos",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Four creeks—Little Dry, Bonadelle, Cottonwood, and Root—thread through the area, though none sustain year‑round flow.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
